From 532c4049c7e14caf881060169d1c86750b6baea8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Micka=C3=ABl=20Bourneuf?= <mickael.bourneuf@ameleo.fr>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 14:15:23 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] ui/dbus: don't assert on tex_id when a virtio-gpu-gl
 scanout is torn down

dbus_scanout_texture() asserts tex_id != 0, but on a device reset while in
virgl/GL scanout mode the scanout is being torn down and the function is
called with tex_id == 0, aborting QEMU:

  qemu-system-x86_64: ui/dbus-listener.c:600: dbus_scanout_texture:
  Assertion `tex_id' failed.

Reproducer: a Windows guest whose virtio-gpu (viogpu) driver is upgraded to a
GL/3D version, then reloaded -- the PnP reload resets the device. Backtrace:

  virtio_pci_reset -> virtio_gpu_gl_reset -> virtio_gpu_virgl_reset_scanout
    -> dpy_gfx_replace_surface -> dbus_gl_gfx_switch -> dbus_scanout_texture

Guard tex_id == 0 (nothing to export, keep the current scanout) instead of
aborting on a legitimate reset.
---
 ui/dbus-listener.c | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/ui/dbus-listener.c b/ui/dbus-listener.c
index 5a72c7e..92b6a4f 100644
--- a/ui/dbus-listener.c
+++ b/ui/dbus-listener.c
@@ -618,7 +618,14 @@ static void dbus_scanout_texture(DisplayChangeListener *dcl,
     uint32_t offset[DMABUF_MAX_PLANES], stride[DMABUF_MAX_PLANES], fourcc;
     uint64_t modifier;
 
-    assert(tex_id);
+    if (!tex_id) {
+        /*
+         * No texture: the scanout is being torn down (e.g. the guest reset
+         * the virtio-gpu device on a driver reload). Nothing to export, keep
+         * the current scanout rather than aborting.
+         */
+        return;
+    }
     if (!egl_dmabuf_export_texture(tex_id, fd, (EGLint *)offset, (EGLint *)stride,
                                    (EGLint *)&fourcc, &num_planes, &modifier)) {
         error_report("%s: failed to export dmabuf for texture", __func__);
